# Revoked release tag signers (Round 38, D2-5). Read by
# .github/scripts/release-gate.sh tag-signature, from release.yml (the tagged
# commit's copy) and from release-guard.yml (main's copy, on every Release
# run). A tag signed by a key listed here is refused even if the key is still
# in .github/allowed_signers and inside its validity window.
#
# One public key per line, exactly as in the key's .pub file:
#
#   ssh-ed25519 AAAA... comment
#
# To revoke a key (lost, leaked, or its holder left), in ONE pull request to
# main: add its public key here, and in .github/allowed_signers either delete
# its line or end it with valid-before="YYYYMMDD" (keeping the line shows
# which tags it once signed). Never delete a line from this file: a revocation
# is permanent. Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored; the file
# must exist (a missing list stops every release).
